OL,3,AAviation faces hotter, stormier skies `
OL,4,Aand passengers might have to accept
OL,5,Amore disruption
OL,6,
OL,7,FAviation faces hotter, stormier skies `
OL,8,Fand passengers might have to accept
OL,9,Fmore disruption
OL,11,FAs the country sweltered through one of
OL,12,Fthe many heatwaves of a baking summer
OL,13,Fin late June, towering thunderclouds
OL,14,Fwere gathering over the south of
OL,15,FEngland and across much of northern
OL,16,FEurope. It was a Saturday, and with the
OL,17,Fholiday season getting under way,
OL,18,Fthousands of passengers were heading to
OL,19,FLondon's Heathrow and Gatwick airports
OL,20,Fto catch flights abroad. It was always
OL,21,Fgoing to be a very busy day.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/3
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
FL,113,105,200,300,0,100
PN,11202
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F112A1788749734
OL,1,W5j 5Qw;j 5wsjj#5wsjs1ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%,.** %-,(,%,. (,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AAviation faces hotter, stormier skies `
OL,4,Aand passengers might have to accept
OL,5,Amore disruption
OL,6,
OL,7,FWhat followed, however, was chaos for
OL,8,Ftravellers. As air traffic controllers
OL,9,Fstruggled to route aircraft around the
OL,10,Fstorms, airspace became heavily
OL,11,Fcongested and many planes due to fly
OL,12,Fwere simply forced to wait on the
OL,13,Fground. In the end, some 900 flights to
OL,14,Fand from both airports were delayed,
OL,15,Fsome by up to 11 hours. Dozens more
OL,16,Fwere cancelled. At airports across
OL,17,FEurope, passengers expecting to fly
OL,18,Finto London also faced long waits and
OL,19,Funcertainty.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/3
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
FL,113,105,200,300,0,100
PN,11203
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F112A1788749734
OL,1,W5j 5Qw;j 5wsjj#5wsjs1ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%,.** %-,(,%,. (,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AAviation faces hotter, stormier skies `
OL,4,Aand passengers might have to accept
OL,5,Amore disruption
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe weather in the UK may now have
OL,8,Fcooled, and passengers may soon forget
OL,9,Ftheir experiences. But some within the
OL,10,Findustry believe what happened in June
OL,11,Fshould be seen as a warning.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/3
